EXT. PAGODA ROOFTOP, FLOODED RICE PADDIES - DAWN

Mist on black water. A cracked tiled roof. Five soldiers pressed flat against it.

SERGEANT OKONKWO, 40s, broad, calm, scans the treeline with binoculars. Beside him, PRIVATE LINDQVIST, 19, pale, hugs a radio like a baby.

Quiet.

CORPORAL HAYASHI, 30s, sniper, wiry, settles behind her rifle. Below, MARCHETTI, 20s, loud even in whispers, drags a crate of ammunition up the slope and spills three boxes, which clatter down the tiles, while Okonkwo grabs Lindqvist's collar to stop him sliding after them and Hayashi swears under her breath and Marchetti dives, catching one box, losing the other two. They splash into the paddy. Ripples spread.

Silence. Everyone holds.

MARCHETTI
(whispering)
Sorry. Sorry.

OKONKWO
Be quiet.

A crack. Far off. A bullet chips a tile beside Lindqvist's head.

Everyone flattens. Radio hisses. Lindqvist fumbles it.

LINDQVIST
They've seen us. They've seen us.

OKONKWO
Good. Let them look at me.

He stands. Raises one hand. Waves at the mist.

HAYASHI
Sergeant --

Nothing. A long breath. The mist stays still.

Then a white scarf, tied to a stick, rises from the far tree line. Waves slowly.

OKONKWO
Hold fire.

MARCHETTI
It's a trick.

HAYASHI
It's a kid. A kid with a scarf.

Lindqvist laughs, one wet hiccup. Marchetti sinks onto the tiles. Hayashi lowers her rifle one inch.

A second crack. Closer. The scarf drops out of sight.

Everyone is moving again. Hayashi up on one knee, Okonkwo hauling Lindqvist back by the strap, Marchetti sliding down the far side toward the water, the radio shrieking static in Lindqvist's arms, and a third shot ringing off the bronze bell above.

OKONKWO
Down! Down the back!

Lindqvist slides. Marchetti catches him. They hit the water together.

Mist closes over the roof.

Silence again. One tile, rocking. Then still.
